[{:db/id "q-109111/selection/2d6cfdfd554881720879744154242fb5aa6f8fe5d2ee6c2ca18d39657060f0e9" :answer/id #uuid "ca6aab5c-9410-5286-9b89-0c2cf34300f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109111/selection/6480237784d6a35fde632a25d557390f228c753685f740cff4c4f9a721c0ce09" :answer/id #uuid "dd3794f3-c6de-538b-89c7-61ce2df8986a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109111/selection/5fc7cbe966d3cf2e947770df4cd8d438a499f70393e26bb13d3308c15c3fe61e" :answer/id #uuid "3c393ebe-ffae-5357-b5c2-2303d5da7402" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109111/selection/01742d8d509ff2ab4085a1ba4b2716ce55d57d0197edc5e28b3b6fd2e7e57977" :answer/id #uuid "3bd2d98e-22f1-5e9f-8afa-ac68a4546b04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109111/selection/85abe6323fb17d3528cb41e333e484a220f40de73de0ade5b121284eb6b9769f" :answer/id #uuid "df266f08-0254-5796-a91e-32108a90b5ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109111/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ef2a47c5-765b-5060-969a-a3cd21ed2b5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109111/selection/85abe6323fb17d3528cb41e333e484a220f40de73de0ade5b121284eb6b9769f" :answer-field/choices ["q-109111/selection/2d6cfdfd554881720879744154242fb5aa6f8fe5d2ee6c2ca18d39657060f0e9" "q-109111/selection/6480237784d6a35fde632a25d557390f228c753685f740cff4c4f9a721c0ce09" "q-109111/selection/5fc7cbe966d3cf2e947770df4cd8d438a499f70393e26bb13d3308c15c3fe61e" "q-109111/selection/01742d8d509ff2ab4085a1ba4b2716ce55d57d0197edc5e28b3b6fd2e7e57977" "q-109111/selection/85abe6323fb17d3528cb41e333e484a220f40de73de0ade5b121284eb6b9769f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109111" :question/id #uuid "840761dd-7cb5-59cb-8d00-6023949589a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-109111" :question/problem "Consider the triangle $C$ in the plane with vertices $(-1,0),(1,0)$ and $(0,1),$ and the region $D$ bounded by $C.$ According to Green's theorem, \n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}{y}^{2}\\,dx+3xy\\,dy={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nCalculate the function $f(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061381/assets/0dfe132146c4095954d6b628b055317c975fed6ec429b9ad48b68f4015d6c033.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)={y}^{2}$ and $Q(x,y)=3xy.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=3y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}{y}^{2}\\,dx+xy\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3y-2y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f(x,y)=y.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-109111/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf385144-2f48-5874-8c0d-dec31d8fc6e3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109111"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109114/selection/f6bcbb6a2a11045727f27abab4aa32365c2e20e814a4a38fe7654cc2db618714" :answer/id #uuid "4d073f60-8d10-5832-b93b-ff0d4fa83872" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-2x){e}^{xy}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109114/selection/b919a72a2ea188bc96f3d73b42513948004a0bc8bfc7ca24d7989ad21b6640cd" :answer/id #uuid "2dfe4906-c610-55c5-a8a4-83f3f7ee80af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x{y}^{2}{e}^{xy}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109114/selection/bb5b56fb0e4223c1b096d53699a193be5457339a35fce9e3e430f606917466e2" :answer/id #uuid "cb091942-7d84-5db1-a4b5-2095dbda37b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-x{y}^{2}{e}^{xy}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109114/selection/1f871055e4c36d973e1a85e26e00955f8d591ec451533d78b46b9cbf0a378bf1" :answer/id #uuid "fd4a919d-2d44-59f8-be2c-6165664e9787" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2x-y){e}^{xy}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109114/selection/76ff98b741c6807a247909e89d41293acfa3603ce120fab1c697941505fcfb3a" :answer/id #uuid "33f77250-8ade-50a1-9bce-84e0919b6223" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(xy-{y}^{2}){e}^{xy}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109114/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6de1b93d-bbc6-54ab-af34-9e4b5c72294a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109114/selection/b919a72a2ea188bc96f3d73b42513948004a0bc8bfc7ca24d7989ad21b6640cd" :answer-field/choices ["q-109114/selection/f6bcbb6a2a11045727f27abab4aa32365c2e20e814a4a38fe7654cc2db618714" "q-109114/selection/b919a72a2ea188bc96f3d73b42513948004a0bc8bfc7ca24d7989ad21b6640cd" "q-109114/selection/bb5b56fb0e4223c1b096d53699a193be5457339a35fce9e3e430f606917466e2" "q-109114/selection/1f871055e4c36d973e1a85e26e00955f8d591ec451533d78b46b9cbf0a378bf1" "q-109114/selection/76ff98b741c6807a247909e89d41293acfa3603ce120fab1c697941505fcfb3a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109114" :question/id #uuid "373bf35a-f882-57a8-91c1-93858fadb2fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-109114" :question/problem "Consider the quadrilateral $C$ in the plane with vertices $(0,0),(1,0),(1,1)$ and $(0,2),$ and the region $D$ bounded by $C.$ According to Green's theorem, \n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}{y}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\,dx+2xy{e}^{xy}\\,dy={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nCalculate the function $f(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061381/assets/b7fad52bdf54c0870ad4c4939a314f5657e390b589faf76e60a8d8ef5d926039.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)={y}^{2}{e}^{xy}$ and $Q(x,y)=2xy{e}^{xy}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=(2y+x{y}^{2}){e}^{xy},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=(2y+2x{y}^{2}){e}^{xy}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}{y}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\,dx+2xy{e}^{xy}\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[(2y+2x{y}^{2}){e}^{xy}-(2y+x{y}^{2}){e}^{xy}]\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2y+2x{y}^{2}-2y-x{y}^{2}){e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x{y}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f(x,y)=x{y}^{2}{e}^{xy}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-109114/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf385144-2f48-5874-8c0d-dec31d8fc6e3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109114"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186133991 :question/answer-fields 17592186130509] {:db/id "q-108588/selection/ma-v1/e2a04b7354146aa4d3f64a22e26f5e64e6a007bad6f3af4a819e164345087c5f/54c3ba11f08329342e1ac3a32e3f07576c79840bd5c320e7633307672cb2466a" :answer/id #uuid "a3b378e1-1c6a-580e-afaf-70c538fd8c26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(x+y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108588/selection/ma-v1/e2a04b7354146aa4d3f64a22e26f5e64e6a007bad6f3af4a819e164345087c5f/4d9512c126be362129ab373b4f52d1063989bec37c95b1c5767441a945c652e1" :answer/id #uuid "d1a4a1cf-3357-5778-8aeb-f2a2995fc5d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(y-x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108588/selection/ma-v1/e2a04b7354146aa4d3f64a22e26f5e64e6a007bad6f3af4a819e164345087c5f/ecda4a0ea6c971cf59b4d24a2729d7df55995423fc870438818e4950de3a6205" :answer/id #uuid "d73c410e-4300-5aeb-9be0-6e9f964f3d3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108588/selection/ma-v1/e2a04b7354146aa4d3f64a22e26f5e64e6a007bad6f3af4a819e164345087c5f/7c6138ae433016a3ffa13bd1fb8d71dc967f6af23dd661be968515294da802b5" :answer/id #uuid "e902bb33-7013-56f8-b26b-1c735f923cfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}({y}^{3}+{x}^{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108588/selection/ma-v1/e2a04b7354146aa4d3f64a22e26f5e64e6a007bad6f3af4a819e164345087c5f/f3c586562a6732272c2edec0d1fa7b846b11adfaa5ac1304ebd28a99acbff114" :answer/id #uuid "4c34a244-11ca-5569-aa54-e5db0629f83e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(x-y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108588/selection/ma-v1/e2a04b7354146aa4d3f64a22e26f5e64e6a007bad6f3af4a819e164345087c5f" :answer-field/id #uuid "05b7ee70-3230-5a5b-a1e1-f230a06a6b9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-108588/selection/ma-v1/e2a04b7354146aa4d3f64a22e26f5e64e6a007bad6f3af4a819e164345087c5f/f3c586562a6732272c2edec0d1fa7b846b11adfaa5ac1304ebd28a99acbff114" :answer-field/choices ["q-108588/selection/ma-v1/e2a04b7354146aa4d3f64a22e26f5e64e6a007bad6f3af4a819e164345087c5f/54c3ba11f08329342e1ac3a32e3f07576c79840bd5c320e7633307672cb2466a" "q-108588/selection/ma-v1/e2a04b7354146aa4d3f64a22e26f5e64e6a007bad6f3af4a819e164345087c5f/4d9512c126be362129ab373b4f52d1063989bec37c95b1c5767441a945c652e1" "q-108588/selection/ma-v1/e2a04b7354146aa4d3f64a22e26f5e64e6a007bad6f3af4a819e164345087c5f/ecda4a0ea6c971cf59b4d24a2729d7df55995423fc870438818e4950de3a6205" "q-108588/selection/ma-v1/e2a04b7354146aa4d3f64a22e26f5e64e6a007bad6f3af4a819e164345087c5f/7c6138ae433016a3ffa13bd1fb8d71dc967f6af23dd661be968515294da802b5" "q-108588/selection/ma-v1/e2a04b7354146aa4d3f64a22e26f5e64e6a007bad6f3af4a819e164345087c5f/f3c586562a6732272c2edec0d1fa7b846b11adfaa5ac1304ebd28a99acbff114"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-108588"] :question/problem "Consider the square $C$ in the plane with vertices $(0,0),(0,1),(1,0)$ and $(1,1),$ and the region $D$ bounded by $C.$ According to Green's theorem, \n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}{y}^{2}\\,dx+{x}^{2}\\,dy={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is traversed counterclockwise. Calculate the function $f(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061381/assets/aa60dd35a920d166f7cc3238a366bde93bd2c33e1b39b0a38313ab46a8de2d8b.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)={y}^{2}$ and $Q(x,y)={x}^{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}{y}^{2}\\,dx+{x}^{2}\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2x-2y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2(x-y)\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f(x,y)=2(x-y).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-108588/selection/ma-v1/e2a04b7354146aa4d3f64a22e26f5e64e6a007bad6f3af4a819e164345087c5f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-109161"] :question/problem "Consider the path $C,$ in the plane, as the boundary of the region enclosed by the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ and the region $D$ bounded by $C.$ According to Green's theorem, \n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2y\\,dx+{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2y\\,dy={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is traversed counterclockwise. Calculate the function $f(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061381/assets/c44b320dd7ba2824ae0024a3d77d0c6cd6e06fa5889e23879f3d6f464c3a80df.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2y$ and $Q(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2y.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-2{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2y\\,dx+{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2y\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2y-(-2{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2y)]\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2y+2{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2y\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f(x,y)=3{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2y.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-109112/selection/f5caebf80a20f7785d8892d7897ab333777840bcc5b7a491f01715219c970086" :answer/id #uuid "7ebd8e4f-93fd-596a-9767-e04e33363c61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109112/selection/d5ccc67a0af7ed709899adf357dd9d87e71344eb5b1aa1680a11724ea1238f78" :answer/id #uuid "4509c12b-f309-54bd-91a6-b746f47caa94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109112/selection/764070d1123d8d80bf87471980a7114c1ea17b2e2d195997d58a5df4fc9ae51c" :answer/id #uuid "270a3a57-e22d-55c3-9334-4e421e0c0f16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109112/selection/592ed15c1b2f2bd1d36634aa015178cb1a62dba67be3cd4d2a614689ed46186c" :answer/id #uuid "79570551-0734-5c0b-8c2d-44ca8d81412c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109112/selection/2a3e6470b48905513acc4c421fd5a5068d59956267aa8241a6d13261c4900848" :answer/id #uuid "15419b8a-1912-5436-a3ab-3230480a2116" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109112/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "67d0db4d-04ec-55b8-8db6-941083cf71e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109112/selection/d5ccc67a0af7ed709899adf357dd9d87e71344eb5b1aa1680a11724ea1238f78" :answer-field/choices ["q-109112/selection/f5caebf80a20f7785d8892d7897ab333777840bcc5b7a491f01715219c970086" "q-109112/selection/d5ccc67a0af7ed709899adf357dd9d87e71344eb5b1aa1680a11724ea1238f78" "q-109112/selection/764070d1123d8d80bf87471980a7114c1ea17b2e2d195997d58a5df4fc9ae51c" "q-109112/selection/592ed15c1b2f2bd1d36634aa015178cb1a62dba67be3cd4d2a614689ed46186c" "q-109112/selection/2a3e6470b48905513acc4c421fd5a5068d59956267aa8241a6d13261c4900848"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109112" :question/id #uuid "c4b2f939-bcbe-57d3-adca-dd40d50dfdce" :question/math-academy-id "q-109112" :question/problem "Consider the rectangle $C$ in the plane with vertices $(0,0),(2,0),(2,1)$ and $(0,1),$ and the region $D$ bounded by $C.$ According to Green's theorem, \n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}(y\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-{x}^{2}y)\\,dx+(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,dy={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nCalculate the function $f(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061381/assets/8d57fb7f6b8e2e822a11f11a0267994c449c37b43df167a8d48ab8036854b8dd.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-{x}^{2}y$ and $Q(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-{x}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}(y\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-{x}^{2}y)\\,dx+(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-{x}^{2})]\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f(x,y)={x}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-109112/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf385144-2f48-5874-8c0d-dec31d8fc6e3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109112"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-42107/selection/1a7cc6aad88c50251e360e0c90e1c6296eb641eff5fd9cf1aa4fb0cca8c397ae" :answer/id #uuid "0f36e145-58db-55be-ad3e-95fd323b3ffe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{y+1}(1+x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\text{ }dx\\,dy" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42107/selection/742e43ae8a72f46604d6131676d7297064c76f0f360d50f145ed48dbbb75fa26" :answer/id #uuid "ad3da2be-ee4b-50e1-9c68-8315dcb2d8b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y+1}(1-x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\text{ }dx\\,dy" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42107/selection/22fa6b01540bc1e7d861eb33893d8e1ee099ab06df3148d109f2a7105f693c26" :answer/id #uuid "e322714e-cf89-5b37-9882-8400000ffb80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{y+1}(1+x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\text{ }dx\\,dy" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42107/selection/edc84cf1ed7364807ad04241f6ed2a1e862624b4b4668b0ec1bf464b07c454fa" :answer/id #uuid "bb9e0ce6-e720-5d21-aa42-413ccd3af748" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{y}(1+x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\text{ }dx\\,dy" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42107/selection/6b9726fe066360c5e02f996a5ff1805c19cd2039ef0ae863c5a28091861fc5c3" :answer/id #uuid "ec46bad5-2528-5fd6-ad2d-1d5f09285be8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y}(1+x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\text{ }dx\\,dy" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42107/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7860034a-ceac-5639-8545-deba4c73609b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-42107/selection/1a7cc6aad88c50251e360e0c90e1c6296eb641eff5fd9cf1aa4fb0cca8c397ae" :answer-field/choices ["q-42107/selection/1a7cc6aad88c50251e360e0c90e1c6296eb641eff5fd9cf1aa4fb0cca8c397ae" "q-42107/selection/742e43ae8a72f46604d6131676d7297064c76f0f360d50f145ed48dbbb75fa26" "q-42107/selection/22fa6b01540bc1e7d861eb33893d8e1ee099ab06df3148d109f2a7105f693c26" "q-42107/selection/edc84cf1ed7364807ad04241f6ed2a1e862624b4b4668b0ec1bf464b07c454fa" "q-42107/selection/6b9726fe066360c5e02f996a5ff1805c19cd2039ef0ae863c5a28091861fc5c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-42107" :question/id #uuid "95adc28f-4c53-5d2d-9483-596d09977402" :question/math-academy-id "q-42107" :question/problem "Consider the triangle $C$ in the plane with vertices $(0,0),(0,-1)$ and $(1,0),$ and the region $D$ bounded by $C.$ Express ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr,$  where $F(x,y)=⟨x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y⟩,$ as a repeated integral." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061381/assets/6d4f13abad5cc193dccedee3114fbd9cbd9fb8e6b5b3ddb0d07f0ed2ed51f4ff.png)\n\nFirst, notice that we can rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr={∮}_{C}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,dx+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dy\n$$\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ and $Q(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type II region as follows:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):0\\le x\\le y+1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's Theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,dx+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{y+1}(1+x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\text{ }dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-42107/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "48652211-e469-55b9-96cb-2526a4135d34"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42107"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109254/selection/12e324cb9efef1aff4d78a2d8a072062b01a6b4eede8ce294ada7785d6fb9e60" :answer/id #uuid "eec591a5-9725-59ba-9f3e-155f090f1f81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}(1+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109254/selection/f85fc2fa053428bbf364f21256de57826397b96ec55f1dc3a86244d494631637" :answer/id #uuid "09b8c366-f7ae-56ee-a696-f10a9efb7c28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109254/selection/97f8d3d833cf22df381f9a0361675ffcf691f545aa39df2c455bc48e3024d40c" :answer/id #uuid "d92f9b00-e280-587b-8f88-a00f06b8448c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109254/selection/a3a3a7e5ad1bfefde751c1f3851c01b41889c28c36f778be79a564b8800ff9fd" :answer/id #uuid "2c9c4389-a42f-5092-94ba-85897e5a9c73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109254/selection/3213b7a4384998f0ca504db3a69cd8a984d94229e28718b83d1d4fd820829ada" :answer/id #uuid "419f7d57-8076-5b50-a685-73ebcce09f5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109254/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "52c07f15-4e19-51a7-aa31-e2ea2ff17928" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109254/selection/f85fc2fa053428bbf364f21256de57826397b96ec55f1dc3a86244d494631637" :answer-field/choices ["q-109254/selection/12e324cb9efef1aff4d78a2d8a072062b01a6b4eede8ce294ada7785d6fb9e60" "q-109254/selection/f85fc2fa053428bbf364f21256de57826397b96ec55f1dc3a86244d494631637" "q-109254/selection/97f8d3d833cf22df381f9a0361675ffcf691f545aa39df2c455bc48e3024d40c" "q-109254/selection/a3a3a7e5ad1bfefde751c1f3851c01b41889c28c36f778be79a564b8800ff9fd" "q-109254/selection/3213b7a4384998f0ca504db3a69cd8a984d94229e28718b83d1d4fd820829ada"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109254" :question/id #uuid "ec0b1748-e212-5d96-8358-0b705e724a9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-109254" :question/problem "Consider the closed curve $C,$ which is the boundary of the region enclosed by the unit circle and the coordinate axes in the first quadrant. Express ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr,$  where $F(x,y)=⟨y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,x-{e}^{-{y}^{2}}⟩,$ as a repeated integral." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061381/assets/e48034aed1f41cf1f9b30c057186879233fe05cd2ba720dcee436398a732b6ce.png)\n\nFirst, notice that we can rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr={∮}_{C}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,dx+(x-{e}^{-{y}^{2}})\\,dy\n$$\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $Q(x,y)=x-{e}^{-{y}^{2}}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's Theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,dx+(x-{e}^{-{y}^{2}})\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109254/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "48652211-e469-55b9-96cb-2526a4135d34"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109254"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109263/selection/13d85a44eeb71f7a8865ef9ad19db45dba242e71ccb7bcc3d655c74b33d1db38" :answer/id #uuid "ac6ceaee-4a2d-50e4-832a-caa63d321684" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-{x}^{2}}^{x+2}2(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109263/selection/53d70c162e7e59ddb637ce149693ac50eaf5b8de3eadfc1e3b1aa7d0fe74d927" :answer/id #uuid "8a233259-195c-5ede-aba6-03b683d14b49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x+2}2(x-y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109263/selection/1fa004c389f2cb2434e76db09d33eaa206d799d2048baa783abfa3a07197a488" :answer/id #uuid "71d6643f-530b-53ef-b345-a0a3bd6a9d1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x+2}(2y-x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109263/selection/207c35c272811f93e79abdd36b88992d3d05535ffefe9523f345184746c3973d" :answer/id #uuid "f0e36259-d784-5470-a4ef-51a121d23e58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x+2}2(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109263/selection/d323f8aa660fdee9e0d9673eac6560959301800624b79bfc42e2db20acc16663" :answer/id #uuid "875b9ea1-38d2-5e39-88c4-1e7ceec402ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}+x+2}2(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109263/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "991b5390-3ab8-5b4d-9c84-44b1646d58ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109263/selection/207c35c272811f93e79abdd36b88992d3d05535ffefe9523f345184746c3973d" :answer-field/choices ["q-109263/selection/13d85a44eeb71f7a8865ef9ad19db45dba242e71ccb7bcc3d655c74b33d1db38" "q-109263/selection/53d70c162e7e59ddb637ce149693ac50eaf5b8de3eadfc1e3b1aa7d0fe74d927" "q-109263/selection/1fa004c389f2cb2434e76db09d33eaa206d799d2048baa783abfa3a07197a488" "q-109263/selection/207c35c272811f93e79abdd36b88992d3d05535ffefe9523f345184746c3973d" "q-109263/selection/d323f8aa660fdee9e0d9673eac6560959301800624b79bfc42e2db20acc16663"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109263" :question/id #uuid "ee280347-8c9a-5f0b-8ae2-75a94f990bab" :question/math-academy-id "q-109263" :question/problem "Consider the closed curve $C,$ which is the boundary of the region enclosed by the curves $y={x}^{2}$ and $y=x+2.$ Express ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr,$  where $F(x,y)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+x)-{y}^{2},{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}⟩,$ as a repeated integral." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061381/assets/e32b8e7d6ce80d7cedad928f9a2f7acc3c3d7f06add7909e856db27d154068d6.png)\n\nFirst, notice that we can rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr={∮}_{C}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+x)-{y}^{2})\\,dx+({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,dy\n$$\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+x)-{y}^{2}$ and $Q(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-2y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le x+2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's Theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x)-{y}^{2})\\,dx+({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2x+2y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x+2}2(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-109263/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "48652211-e469-55b9-96cb-2526a4135d34"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109263"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109291/selection/7da1743a9f2918ce5fd41eccd30540d887dd955efceef1f8cb5d6525bd56cd0b" :answer/id #uuid "54566b29-f04f-55e0-b35a-9fdd7cb331aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x-1}^{-2x+2}y\\text{ }dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109291/selection/48a76f04d022da6cd734e1fe75bacb786954054b71b60d299f76c4faa08f832d" :answer/id #uuid "46feb382-e198-53ec-846e-167020db95a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x-1}^{-2x+2}(y+4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{ }dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109291/selection/458238223ca4be2e1aaf4ec4415545a28fd5df8c8b10ea45af4e3354abb9b999" :answer/id #uuid "65855edd-ff16-5542-885c-f4ba18b44d2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{-2x+2}y\\text{ }dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109291/selection/de0824d043afe6890fdc1f01692aee38e84d6f4960df0c60203060253863719d" :answer/id #uuid "d7ca2fc9-7023-5282-aab8-0ff034b70973" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x-1}^{-2x+2}(x-(2+{y}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\text{ }dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109291/selection/c8c6e1c2d87814ff0b266773f627ef3ea6732bda8cc02ad91cd96dd199152ac3" :answer/id #uuid "1a738a4d-8566-5bdb-a6e3-86db9d0c235e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{x+1}^{-2x+2}y\\text{ }dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109291/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f53d5d9f-7c77-5108-b98b-9fc856f7cb89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109291/selection/7da1743a9f2918ce5fd41eccd30540d887dd955efceef1f8cb5d6525bd56cd0b" :answer-field/choices ["q-109291/selection/7da1743a9f2918ce5fd41eccd30540d887dd955efceef1f8cb5d6525bd56cd0b" "q-109291/selection/48a76f04d022da6cd734e1fe75bacb786954054b71b60d299f76c4faa08f832d" "q-109291/selection/458238223ca4be2e1aaf4ec4415545a28fd5df8c8b10ea45af4e3354abb9b999" "q-109291/selection/de0824d043afe6890fdc1f01692aee38e84d6f4960df0c60203060253863719d" "q-109291/selection/c8c6e1c2d87814ff0b266773f627ef3ea6732bda8cc02ad91cd96dd199152ac3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109291" :question/id #uuid "d02b88c9-898d-50c4-a59e-b0f309ffc0a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-109291" :question/problem "Consider the triangle $C$ in the plane with vertices $(0,-1),(1,0)$ and $(0,2),$ and the region $D$ bounded by $C.$ Express ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr,$  where $F(x,y)=⟨{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,xy-2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x⟩,$ as a repeated integral." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061381/assets/c2e08c233cb31124234ab6e5179998a3bdc148024632c7770bdea46cd37dff83.png)\n\nFirst, notice that we can rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr={∮}_{C}{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dx+(xy-2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,dy\n$$\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)={y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $Q(x,y)=xy-2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=y+2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):0\\le x\\le 1,\\,x-1\\le y\\le -2x+2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's Theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dx+(xy-2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(y+2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x-1}^{-2x+2}y\\text{ }dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109291/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "48652211-e469-55b9-96cb-2526a4135d34"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109291"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-108467"] :question/problem "Consider the triangle $C$ in the plane with vertices $(0,0),(1,0)$ and $(1,2),$ traversed counterclockwise, and the region $D$ bounded by $C.$ Express ${∮}_{C}x{y}^{2}\\,dx+2{x}^{2}y\\,dy$ as a repeated integral." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061381/assets/2e63a57e50b60d7f0c6a3ce12d164716e2cba71c6bd4c6df10460a35beba4209.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=x{y}^{2}$ and $Q(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2xy,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=4xy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):0\\le x\\le 1,0\\le y\\le 2x}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's Theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}x{y}^{2}\\,dx+2{x}^{2}y\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(4xy-2xy)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}2xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-109160/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "c4468424-e400-5904-a99b-b17758f9a7b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109160/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "67e72b99-1de1-51ec-9cb8-fc62b3796b3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109160/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "39bf819b-a038-5d9f-8d3b-86af1f7a241f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109160/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "04b7e7e3-ca78-50e0-809f-8b3d3d03a910" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109160/selection/b78cefa051ec62e42babb0396ce415bc1c6b03c29d281d68224ab0312a503d34" :answer/id #uuid "d7d6a01e-c34f-5983-adf9-290b8f1ac849" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109160/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e0ad572f-e943-5498-a564-8675655daeba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109160/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-109160/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-109160/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-109160/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-109160/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" "q-109160/selection/b78cefa051ec62e42babb0396ce415bc1c6b03c29d281d68224ab0312a503d34"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109160" :question/id #uuid "fb32a8d9-aa89-5e27-976f-eafd97e6f9c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-109160" :question/problem "Use Green's theorem to evaluate ${∮}_{C}(2y-x)\\,dx+(5x-y)\\,dy,$ where $C$ is the boundary of the region enclosed by the curves $y=x$ and $y={x}^{2}-x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061381/assets/e788bbcbda4cc715c6989b7de9d08d60e3b0d178eeb9432a342a4c86c4c01b86.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=2y-x$ and $Q(x,y)=5x-y.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):0\\le x\\le 2,\\,{x}^{2}-x\\le y\\le x}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's Theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}(2y-x)\\,dx+(5x-y)\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5-2)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}-x}^{x}\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}[y]_{{x}^{2}-x}^{x}\\,dx \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2x-{x}^{2})\\,dx \\\\  & =3{[{x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =3(4-\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-109160/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11d3f9e1-dad0-51d4-86a9-e0c49465cc3c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109160"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109164/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "80a6444e-fc55-5591-b399-ca0688eae1e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109164/selection/c7afbfc2e89be80ce595330a13dddefcaf8ec1ef626a89c078820c5064f3c793" :answer/id #uuid "5f153383-2fe2-58b7-9b84-bab4e991f500" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{41}{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109164/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" :answer/id #uuid "ffa389a3-d361-5ae0-bea8-234757030082" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109164/selection/b759b6655248e4e5495c684d2618cb276256102f7a0cdbbf39ead1b11c1f5701" :answer/id #uuid "3666d6cc-e324-547c-a228-4aea9f7581f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{81}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109164/selection/41a9c7d10a5fad5a7019c6d5ffb8325f34ce82e3530aea159abb2d35b495aca8" :answer/id #uuid "b82b0bdc-b930-5743-8902-204960832819" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{23}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109164/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5229ec56-3f0b-5fa8-86d4-129290e5188e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109164/selection/b759b6655248e4e5495c684d2618cb276256102f7a0cdbbf39ead1b11c1f5701" :answer-field/choices ["q-109164/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-109164/selection/c7afbfc2e89be80ce595330a13dddefcaf8ec1ef626a89c078820c5064f3c793" "q-109164/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" "q-109164/selection/b759b6655248e4e5495c684d2618cb276256102f7a0cdbbf39ead1b11c1f5701" "q-109164/selection/41a9c7d10a5fad5a7019c6d5ffb8325f34ce82e3530aea159abb2d35b495aca8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109164" :question/id #uuid "5a6dc375-a6eb-5992-aad2-4ef3ba82fede" :question/math-academy-id "q-109164" :question/problem "Use Green's theorem to evaluate ${∮}_{C}2xy\\,dx+{y}^{2}\\,dy,$ where $C$ is the boundary of the region enclosed by the curves $y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}$ and $y=\\sqrt{3x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061381/assets/eb0b120cc4d63c8dab18c8acb37f5835e99db746584262f6bb33e8ca99b6a16d.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=2xy$ and $Q(x,y)={y}^{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2x,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{3x}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's Theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}2xy\\,dx+{y}^{2}\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(0-2x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/3}^{\\sqrt{3x}}(-2x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(-2x)[y]_{{x}^{2}/3}^{\\sqrt{3x}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(-2x)(\\sqrt{3x}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3})dx \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{0}^{3}(\\sqrt{3}{x}^{3/2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})dx \\\\  & =-2{[\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{3x}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{12}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{2(3)^{2}\\sqrt{3(3)}}{5}-\\frac{(3)^{4}}{12}) \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{54}{5}-\\frac{27}{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{81}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-109164/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11d3f9e1-dad0-51d4-86a9-e0c49465cc3c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109164"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-109147"] :question/problem "Use Green's theorem to evaluate ${∮}_{C}({e}^{x}-2{x}^{2}y)\\,dx+({e}^{y}+2x{y}^{2})\\,dy,$ where $C$ is the boundary of the triangle with vertices at $(0,0),$ $(2,2)$ and $(-2,2),$ traversed counterclockwise." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061381/assets/7ca4b6fe3a5a16c4004c75b0e4524cc3b42550cb2413d5b8e1c21a1d53cee902.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)={e}^{x}-2{x}^{2}y$ and $Q(x,y)={e}^{y}+2x{y}^{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-2{x}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =2{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type II region as follows:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):-y\\le x\\le y,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's Theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}({e}^{x}-2{x}^{2}y)\\,dx+({e}^{y}+2x{y}^{2})\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2{y}^{2}+2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-y}^{y}(2{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{-y}^{y}\\,dy \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}+{y}^{3}+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}+{y}^{3})dy \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{8{y}^{3}}{3}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{3}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{[{y}^{4}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot {2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-41811/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" :answer/id #uuid "023a78d9-3652-5259-a852-292d93e71fb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41811/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "b70c91ed-7e50-5684-aa1a-ce4f0f37fc33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41811/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer/id #uuid "57efe768-472c-5f2c-8dba-cab3a5ca79b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41811/selection/95c393685f82efe05ce58fc07554851561d61659fa09076d238e849d9023f203" :answer/id #uuid "dcc584ed-5d2b-5c0f-a536-3a70bc8a2bfd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41811/selection/2aef90071200a7bc65baa2d03f49803233ca7b2dc16865265136281ee914878b" :answer/id #uuid "e2a82101-c28b-5830-81af-b93c42572664" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41811/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f283d133-f208-5ecf-94cb-b68e3328340c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-41811/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer-field/choices ["q-41811/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" "q-41811/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-41811/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" "q-41811/selection/95c393685f82efe05ce58fc07554851561d61659fa09076d238e849d9023f203" "q-41811/selection/2aef90071200a7bc65baa2d03f49803233ca7b2dc16865265136281ee914878b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-41811" :question/id #uuid "02c2afcf-c82c-531e-a25b-5a0c4c7e8242" :question/math-academy-id "q-41811" :question/problem "Use Green's theorem to evaluate ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr,$ where $F(x,y)=⟨{x}^{3}+2{y}^{2},{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y⟩$ and $C$ is the boundary of the triangle with vertices at $(0,0),$ $(2,0)$ and $(1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061381/assets/73bf9b973e50c540a873f4f1a44d936474e4c49d7041a330902508a840645009.png)\n\nFirst, notice that we can rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr={∮}_{C}({x}^{3}+2{y}^{2})\\,dx+({x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)\\,dy\n$$\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)={x}^{3}+2{y}^{2}$ and $Q(x,y)={x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=4y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type II region as follows:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):y\\le x\\le 2-y,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's Theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}({x}^{3}+2{y}^{2})\\,dx+({x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2x-4y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{2-y}(2x-4y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[{x}^{2}-4xy]}_{y}^{2-y}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[(2-y)^{2}-4(2-y)y-{y}^{2}+4{y}^{2}]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(8{y}^{2}-12y+4)\\,dy \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2{y}^{2}-3y+1)\\,dy \\\\  & =4{[\\frac{2{y}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2}+y]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4[\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{3}{2}+1] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-41811/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11d3f9e1-dad0-51d4-86a9-e0c49465cc3c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-41811"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109115/selection/968b78a1da72ee3df196b4b60a1cb9afd2082e522352c24e5babcf63ab6a5c7b" :answer/id #uuid "df0b064a-66d1-5598-b021-2c4ea2befcdd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109115/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "79155285-d146-53af-8186-5ff16e207459" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109115/selection/25666b67a56594dd5245ec05e89d883db07d04362ab51dbc90c39ad20f7f9142" :answer/id #uuid "b5b9b594-f3fb-5769-83c2-0dc1ada2556b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109115/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "b7f89eba-5dc7-5dcb-ad23-c65b74b7bf03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109115/selection/8cf4edd6abdb88922c00414679288e866f4f3f0653d5d908a8c994f8f6e02d92" :answer/id #uuid "e700e60c-e611-565f-b9c2-7b192979a68f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109115/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4de0cfeb-c8e2-5ab1-99a2-9d0e011273b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109115/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-109115/selection/968b78a1da72ee3df196b4b60a1cb9afd2082e522352c24e5babcf63ab6a5c7b" "q-109115/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-109115/selection/25666b67a56594dd5245ec05e89d883db07d04362ab51dbc90c39ad20f7f9142" "q-109115/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-109115/selection/8cf4edd6abdb88922c00414679288e866f4f3f0653d5d908a8c994f8f6e02d92"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109115" :question/id #uuid "f3566a7d-b3b7-5dcf-bd29-b00dd8bc7628" :question/math-academy-id "q-109115" :question/problem "Use Green's theorem to evaluate ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr,$ where $F(x,y)=(3xy-1)\\,i+(3{x}^{2}+{e}^{y})\\,j$ and $C$ is the boundary of the region enclosed by the curves $y=2x$ and $y={x}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061381/assets/5f34ac74599937e0ae181126ff9a3da5b29dfe213614a1f23ca10c7062f22f7d.png)\n\nFirst, notice that we can rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr={∮}_{C}(3xy-1)\\,dx+(3{x}^{2}+{e}^{y})\\,dy\n$$\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=3xy-1$ and $Q(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+{e}^{y}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=3x,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =6x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):0\\le x\\le 2,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 2x}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's Theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}(3xy-1)\\,dx+(3{x}^{2}+{e}^{y})\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(6x-3x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2x}3x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3x[y]_{{x}^{2}}^{2x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3x(2x-{x}^{2})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(6{x}^{2}-3{x}^{3})\\,dx \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3}-\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2(2)^{3}-\\frac{3(2)^{4}}{4} \\\\  & =16-12 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-109115/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11d3f9e1-dad0-51d4-86a9-e0c49465cc3c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109115"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9071"] :question/problem "Consider the triangle $C$ in the plane with vertices $(0,0), (1,0)$ and $(0,2),$ and the region $D$ bounded by $C.$ According to Green's theorem, \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle{\\oint\\limits_{C}\\cos{y}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+x\\sin{y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y}= \\iint\\limits_D f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d A,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is traversed counterclockwise. Calculate the function $f(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\oint\\limits_{C} P\\,\\mathrm{d}x + Q\\,\\mathrm{d}y \n= \\iint\\limits_D \\left(\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} - \\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}\\right)\\,\\textrm d A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061381/assets/a78a98750e3203760d27daaebd42852198538935e2c3777a0b8a8c85d1bb0901.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)= \\cos{y}$ and $Q(x,y)= x\\sin{y}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,dx+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f(x,y) = 2\\sin{y}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9086"] :question/problem "Consider the triangle $C$ in the plane with vertices $(0,0), (1,1)$ and $(-1,1),$ traversed counterclockwise, and the region $D$ bounded by $C.$ Express $\\displaystyle{\\oint\\limits_{C}x\\sin{y}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+ (x^2\\cos{y}-y^2)\\,\\mathrm{d}y}$ as a repeated integral." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\oint\\limits_{C} P\\,\\mathrm{d}x + Q\\,\\mathrm{d}y \n= \\iint\\limits_D \\left(\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} - \\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}\\right)\\,\\textrm d A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061381/assets/2fa3c84359cec5f5e0750552e5a4b24b20b8dbc3d65b909aea908e1505cfb5e3.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)= x\\sin{y}$ and $Q(x,y)= x^2\\cos{y}-y^2.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type II region as follows:\n\n$$\nD = \\{(x,y) :  -y\\leq x\\leq y,\\, 0\\leq y \\leq 1\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's Theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dx+({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-{y}^{2})\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-y}^{y}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9072"] :question/problem "Use Green's theorem to evaluate $\\displaystyle{\\oint\\limits_{C} 4x^2y \\, \\mathrm{d}x+ 2y^2\\,\\mathrm{d}y},$ where $C$ is the boundary of the triangle with vertices at $(0,0),$ $(1,2)$ and $(0,2),$ traversed counterclockwise." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\oint\\limits_{C} P\\,\\mathrm{d}x + Q\\,\\mathrm{d}y \n= \\iint\\limits_D \\left(\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} - \\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}\\right)\\textrm d A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061381/assets/a87f696b1eb42588ab69800b72d821bf47b35676fc19dcd4fe2927bbf36ba3f8.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)= 4x^2y$ and $Q(x,y)= 2y^2.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=4{x}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{(x,y) : 0 \\leq x \\leq 1,\\, 2x \\leq y \\leq 2 \\right\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's Theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}4{x}^{2}y\\,dx+2{y}^{2}\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(0-4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2x}^{2}(-4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-4{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}[y]_{2x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & =-4{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}(2-2x)\\,dx \\\\  & =-8{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}(1-x)\\,dx \\\\  & =-8{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}\\,dx \\\\  & =-8{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-8(\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =-8\\cdot \\frac{1}{12} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
